1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:06,756
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,719
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,060
[Emerson] <i>I have a sighting</i>
<i>of Tailor AFAM.</i>

7
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:21,187
[in English] <i>I already have visuals.</i>
<i>Be alert.</i>

8
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:22,147
[in English] What happened? Are you okay?

9
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,606
[Emerson groans] <i>Pulikat! Pulikat!</i>

10
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,567
[in English] This is for muscles.
Rub it on your muscle, here.

11
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:27,402
Third tree. [coughs]

12
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:30,447
Three trees, past the bridge.

13
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:31,364
[in English] Copy, copy.

14
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,658
[in English] We have news
about Dmitri Regalia.

15
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:34,909
[in English] He is dead.

16
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:36,494
[in English] You'll go to the funeral.

17
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:39,080
[Samir, in English] <i>Audrey</i>
<i>and her daughter will be at the funeral.</i>

18
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:40,790
[in English] <i>You bring them</i>
<i>back to me untouched.</i>

19
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,667
- [Samir, in English] <i>Bring them back.</i>
- [Emerson, in English] <i>Mission abort.</i>

20
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,169
- [Emerson, in English] <i>Mission abort.</i>
- Huh?

21
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:46,171
- [in English] That's Audrey, right?
- [Audrey, in English] Go, go, go, go, go!

22
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,590
[Kurt, in English] He's chasing Mama Mary
and the Adopted Thread!

23
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:49,966
Is that Audrey?!

24
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:51,426
[Mongki] <i>Let's go. We need to get them.</i>

25
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:55,346
[Samir, in English]
Where do you think you are going?

26
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:56,806
[grunting and groaning]

27
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,226
[grunting and groaning]

28
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,811
There is a royal rumble there!

29
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,564
[boy] <i>AFAM versus blond thug</i>

30
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:06,941
<i>versus fat vendor with a bolo!</i>

31
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:08,902
Gavin!

32
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:12,113
[grunting and groaning]

33
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:13,531
[Kurt] Children of the Thread, let's go!

34
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:17,452
[grunting and groaning]

35
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:18,661
[security guard, in English] They're gone.

36
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,622
So, they want to kidnap her
to blackmail Atoy.

37
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:22,832
So, what does that mean? They have Atoy.

38
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:25,543
How do we find out
where Brother Atoy is now?

39
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:27,253
What if we kidnap Samir?

40
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:29,130
Let's save Atoy!

41
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:31,925
[in English] Operation Kidnap AFAM.

42
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:33,635
- [Karla] <i>Let's go!</i>
- [Gavin] <i>Let's go! Let's go!</i>

43
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:34,552
Atoy!

44
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:37,972
After you eat, don't throw away the bone.

45
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:39,140
We can still use it.

46
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:40,892
I can't be the only one eating.

47
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:43,311
[Lily] You should eat too.
You need strength.

48
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:44,521
PREVIOUSLY

49
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:46,314
[music fades]

50
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:48,942
What's new?

51
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:50,652
You failed again.

52
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:56,282
Boss, when we were tracing Olga
at the jogging park earlier,

53
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:59,577
we spotted Audrey with Gavin.

54
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,748
So, they're still together.

55
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:04,916
What were they doing there?

56
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:08,128
Jogging, of course. It's a jogging park.

57
00:02:09,462 --> 00:02:11,923
You're being sarcastic.
Do you want me to replace you?

58
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:14,300
Don't, boss. I still have
a lot of bills to pay.

59
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:17,345
But boss, when we chased them,

60
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:21,057
suddenly, two tall mestizo guys
also tried to kidnap them.

61
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,644
[Mongki] We got in the middle,
of course, but…

62
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:26,479
everyone scattered.

63
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:28,481
[pensive music playing]

64
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:30,984
Looks like Atoy struck
the nerve of other people too.

65
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:34,445
That's good. That might
make our job easier.

66
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:37,365
Just don't let Gavin get dragged in.

67
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,619
It wasn't just those two there, boss.

68
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:44,247
Someone was protecting them.

69
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:48,126
A young man, good at fighting.

70
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:49,752
[tense music playing]

71
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:52,881
He even looks a bit like me,
if I shaved my mustache and beard.

72
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:57,677
So, I'm sure, boss,
those two won't be dealt with easily.

73
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:02,098
[music swells]

74
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:03,391
[music fades]

75
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:06,352
[suave theme music playing]

76
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:09,772
[motorcycle revving]

77
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:10,732
[sewing machine whirring]

78
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:12,650
[scratches]

79
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:13,693
[snipping]

80
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:15,194
[clicking]

81
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:17,572
[sewing machine clacking]

82
00:03:17,655 --> 00:03:19,282
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

83
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:20,950
[gunshots]

84
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:23,244
[clicking]

85
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:24,662
[snipping]

86
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:27,290
[music swells]

87
00:03:27,373 --> 00:03:30,168
[electronic blipping]

88
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:34,422
[music fades]

89
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:37,425
Hey, Ibyang?

90
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:39,010
Hey.

91
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:41,721
Ibyang, what are you doing? It's late.

92
00:03:41,804 --> 00:03:43,681
Shouldn't you be asleep?

93
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:45,725
I was waiting for you, Sister Faye.

94
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:46,851
Me?

95
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:48,561
Mm-hmm.

96
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:54,400
Because I was thinking of…
a gift for Mama.

97
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,111
[in English] Gift? Well…

98
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:58,738
Your mom loves cupcakes.

99
00:03:58,821 --> 00:04:00,531
Maybe that.

100
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:02,450
- [in English] Cupcake?
- Mmm-mm.

101
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:06,496
Oh, I don't have money to buy that.

102
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:10,458
- Sister Faye, maybe…
- What?

103
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,418
- Do you have money?
- Hey.

104
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:13,628
- Please lend me some.
- Hey.

105
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:15,463
Oh my. This kid.

106
00:04:15,546 --> 00:04:18,258
Don't borrow from me
because I don't have money either.

107
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:19,676
- Oh no.
- I have an idea.

108
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:23,680
What if you give your mom
something that comes from the heart?

109
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:25,056
That's priceless.

110
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:26,891
She'll love that more.

111
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:28,142
Ah.

112
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:33,481
[Ibyang] "Tatoy, Tatoy,
even if you're not my real father,

113
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:37,694
in my heart, you're the true hero!"

114
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:40,280
[sentimental music playing]

115
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:42,448
- I know! I know, I know.
- Hmm?

116
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,743
I will just write her a poem!

117
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,120
Oh, hmm…

118
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:50,331
That's also what I gave Tatoy.

119
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:59,132
Don't you miss your Tatoy?

120
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:01,592
Don't you want to go back to him?

121
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:04,595
I miss him.

122
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:09,309
- But Mama needs me.
- Oh…

123
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:17,400
We should be together, but…

124
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:20,278
- I text him.
- Mmm?

125
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:24,365
But he doesn't reply.

126
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:27,410
Oh…

127
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,495
All right. Don't think about that anymore.

128
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:33,499
Here's what you should do.
Get some rest, sleep, because tomorrow,

129
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,251
we'll go out again.

130
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,003
- Do you want that?
- We'll go out again?

131
00:05:37,086 --> 00:05:38,171
Yes.

132
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:40,840
But we just went out earlier.

133
00:05:40,923 --> 00:05:45,636
You… You're really pesky.
Come on. Go inside.

134
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,263
- Come on.
- Okay.

135
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:49,307
Come on. Go inside.

136
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,476
You know what we'll do, right?

137
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:55,229
[in English] So, let's work
on the disguise requirements.

138
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:59,358
[Kurt] And ask right away,
so we can finalize everything

139
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:00,902
before we leave tomorrow.

140
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:02,695
- [Kurt, in English] Okay?
- [in English] Okay.

141
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:06,240
[Ame] Brother Kurt,
please message Emerson.

142
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:09,744
Tell him to also buy batteries
for our earpieces.

143
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:11,704
I'll take care of that.

144
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:14,791
I'll get the whole team new earpieces.

145
00:06:14,874 --> 00:06:16,209
[pensive music playing]

146
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:19,504
That's why you're my ace.

147
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:21,923
- Right, Karla?
- [Karla] Huh?

148
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:27,095
Karla, maybe you shouldn't come.

149
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:28,262
It's dangerous.

150
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:30,973
Something… Something bad
might happen to you.

151
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:34,310
Mom, don't think negatively.

152
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:37,647
You saw it, right?
We're planning this thoroughly.

153
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:40,066
I can handle myself.

154
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:42,985
One more thing.

155
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:46,322
This is not the first time I'm joining
a mission with Brother Atoy.

156
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:48,699
I can help.

157
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:52,120
Miss Cita, don't worry.

158
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:54,580
I'll take care of Karla.

159
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:58,334
I won't let anything happen to her,
and I'll bring her home safe.

160
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:00,795
I'm nervous.

161
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:01,879
[clears throat]

162
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:05,424
Miss Cita, you can also count on me.

163
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:06,926
I'll protect Karla.

164
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:08,970
I won't abandon my friend.

165
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:13,766
[sneaky music playing]

166
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:14,892
Ouch!

167
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:17,395
- [Uno] Why? What happened?
- Oh, wow, Karla.

168
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:19,480
Your hair is so long.

169
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:20,898
It reaches up to here.

170
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:23,025
- Fix it!
- You know what? Let's just sleep.

171
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,861
We have a mission tomorrow, right?

172
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,446
- Let's take a rest now.
- [Ame] Come on, Mom!

173
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:27,363
- [Ame] Fix your hair first.
- Let's go.

174
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:28,322
[Ame] Oh, it's on the floor now.

175
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:29,949
- Let's go, let's go.
- [Ame] It reached here. [giggles]

176
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:37,874
[upbeat music playing]

177
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:40,042
[music fades]

178
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:43,838
[sinister music playing]

179
00:07:52,388 --> 00:07:55,475
[indistinct chattering]

180
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:56,851
[in English] Uh, excuse me.

181
00:07:56,934 --> 00:08:00,354
[in English] Can you tell me the way
to the rondalla performance at 6:30 p.m.?

182
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:01,689
[chuckles] <i>Buenas noches!</i>

183
00:08:01,772 --> 00:08:03,357
<i>Noches buenas!</i>

184
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:05,651
[in Spanish] That's great.
You speak Spanish?

185
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:08,196
[in English] Uh, no, señora.

186
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:10,615
[in English] We don't really
speak Spanish fluently.

187
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:11,908
[in English] Yes, uh…

188
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:14,952
[in English] Only Spanish words
I know, uh…

189
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:16,746
[in English] Spanish bread.

190
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:19,332
[in English] Uh, Spanish sardines.

191
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:22,126
<i>Hola! Señora.</i>

192
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,629
<i>Cuchara, atchara.</i>

193
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:25,963
Maribeth Bichara.

194
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:27,757
<i>Sayonara.</i>

195
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:31,928
[in English] Uh, anyway, just go down,
and then turn right.

196
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:34,305
[in English] Then, just follow the signs
of the rondalla performance.

197
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:36,140
- <i>Gracias!</i>
- [Emerson, in English] Yes.

198
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,225
[in English] It means thank you.

199
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,560
<i>Gracias dos.</i>

200
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,145
[in English] Thank you too.

201
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:43,397
[sneaky music playing]

202
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:46,567
This is so hard, isn't it?

203
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:50,112
Turns out when you're in disguise,
you also need to know the language.

204
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:52,240
Why did you even speak Spanish?

205
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:53,366
Eh, eh…

206
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:56,661
We're civil guards, right?
It should be Spanish.

207
00:08:56,744 --> 00:08:59,747
Brother Emerson, next time,
let's just stick to English.

208
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,916
That's the international language anyway.

209
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,585
Come on. I was just trying.

210
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:09,090
And don't call me Brother Emerson here.

211
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:11,592
Thread 1, okay?

212
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,970
Adopted Thread, don't forget.

213
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:16,180
We're here for OKA.

214
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:18,474
[in English] Operation Kidnap AFAM.

215
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:21,852
All right. Go back to your post.
Go back to your post.

216
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:23,437
Go.

217
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:25,273
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

218
00:09:25,356 --> 00:09:27,650
Uh, Thread 1.

219
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:29,068
[Emerson, in English] <i>Hi, everybody.</i>

220
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:30,945
How are your positions? Over.

221
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:33,823
This is itchy.

222
00:09:36,492 --> 00:09:38,202
[in English] This is Thread 2, reporting.

223
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:40,621
I'm itching in this gown.

224
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:44,208
- I don't think I can dance later.
- [clears throat]

225
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:45,626
Karla.

226
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,295
That's called <i>traje de mestiza.</i>

227
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:50,256
Like what Maria Clara wore.

228
00:09:50,339 --> 00:09:53,009
Brother Kurt, it's the same.

229
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,093
It's still itchy.

230
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:58,014
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

231
00:09:58,764 --> 00:09:59,599
- [in English] Hello!
- <i>Hola!</i>

232
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:00,975
Can we take a picture with you?

233
00:10:01,058 --> 00:10:03,936
Of course! With a small fee.

234
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,062
- Joke only, guys.
- [camera shutter snaps]

235
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:06,731
- [in English] Thank you!
- [in English] Thank you.

236
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:08,357
Hey, it's Maria Clara!

237
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,693
<i>Hola! Buenas noches!</i>

238
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:12,987
- Can we take a picture with you?
- [in English] Of course!

239
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:15,781
[in Spanish] Thank you.

240
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:17,575
Uh, you're really…

241
00:10:18,075 --> 00:10:20,244
You're really taking pictures there, huh.

242
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:21,245
- [chuckles softly]
- [music fades]

243
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:23,914
And this is the end of our tour.

244
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:26,500
Thank you for coming.

245
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:28,586
There's also a version in Bataan.

246
00:10:28,669 --> 00:10:31,088
That's the original. Hope you can visit.

247
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:33,382
- [in English] Thank you! Bye!
- [in English] Thank you!

248
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:34,967
- [in English] Thank you.
- Thank you.

249
00:10:36,093 --> 00:10:38,346
[sneaky music playing]

250
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,765
How's your location, Mini Thread?

251
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:43,726
It's fun.

252
00:10:43,809 --> 00:10:47,021
I hope we can come here again,
but not on a mission,

253
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:48,606
but to stroll around.

254
00:10:50,107 --> 00:10:52,735
Sis, are you talking to someone?

255
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:55,279
Oh, I'm just self-talking.

256
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:56,280
It's a trend.

257
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:57,531
Don't you do that?

258
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:00,493
[scoffs]

259
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:04,497
- [music fades]
- Ma'am, buy this, ma'am.

260
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,374
Puppet, ma'am!
It's very affordable, ma'am!

261
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,627
Do your best to sell there, Tape Measure.

262
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,379
But don't sell them all.

263
00:11:11,462 --> 00:11:12,421
Leave one for me,

264
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:14,799
so I can give it to Ibyang
when we see each other.

265
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:16,008
[in English] Roger that.

266
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:17,676
Ma'am, buy this, ma'am!

267
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,720
Nine hundred… Oh, here! Just 500, ma'am.

268
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:22,223
Ma'am, sir, buy this puppet!

269
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:23,516
They're beautiful!

270
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:28,437
Mommy, Daddy, I want this.

271
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:31,107
You want it? It's very pretty!

272
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:32,691
I want that, please!

273
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:33,984
How much for that?

274
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:36,278
It used to be 1,200,

275
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:38,155
but I'll give it to you for 900.

276
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:42,576
This one was 700,
but just 500, sir, for baby.

277
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,036
Okay, we'll take it. Nine hundred.

278
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,746
- [Uno] Really? Okay.
- [kid] Yay!

279
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:47,581
Just be careful. It tangles.

280
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:49,458
But it still dances, look.

281
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:52,670
Like this. See?

282
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:54,088
[in English] Sir.

283
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,631
- Thank you, sir. Here's your change, sir.
- Thank you, brother.

284
00:11:56,507 --> 00:11:58,426
And you were really able
to sell, Tape Measure.

285
00:11:58,509 --> 00:11:59,343
[in English] Yes.

286
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:02,263
I can really sell, Thread 2.

287
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,890
- [sneaky music playing]
- The view here is beautiful.

288
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:05,808
You get it?

289
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:07,601
Huh?

290
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:09,478
Hey, Feeling Thread.

291
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:10,938
Can we focus on work?

292
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:12,481
"Feeling Thread"?

293
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:14,567
I am focused on work.

294
00:12:14,650 --> 00:12:17,653
And there's no Feeling Thread here.

295
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:20,364
FYI. I meant you.

296
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:22,450
Ah.

297
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,869
My codename is Tape Measure.

298
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:25,786
[in English] Stick to that.

299
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:29,206
You're Feeling Thread to me.

300
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:31,667
You…

301
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:33,544
Stop it, stop it.

302
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:35,296
What's wrong with you?

303
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,674
Adopted Thread is right.

304
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:40,009
We need to focus.

305
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:41,802
We're here for…

306
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:44,013
Operation Kidnap AFAM.

307
00:12:44,096 --> 00:12:44,930
So, how's it?

308
00:12:45,014 --> 00:12:47,975
Have you found the location
of Tailor AFAM?

309
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:49,810
- Not yet.
- [in English] Negative.

310
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:50,728
No.

311
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,188
Okay, just…

312
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,523
update me when you see him.

313
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:55,900
Thanks.

314
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:57,109
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

315
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:59,445
- [in English] Copy.
- [in English] Okay.

316
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:00,488
[in English] Roger that.

317
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:01,405
[in English] Yes, ma'am!

318
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:04,950
[music ends]

319
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,870
Brother Emerson, did you buy pepper spray?

320
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:10,372
Uh…

321
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:12,541
Just pepper.

322
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,251
[Emerson] Mmm, no spray.

323
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:15,961
That's fine.

324
00:13:16,045 --> 00:13:17,213
Samir will still get teary-eyed from that.

325
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:19,757
[sneaky music playing]

326
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:23,677
So, what if Samir doesn't come here?

327
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:25,554
What if he suddenly decides
to go to Boracay?

328
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,390
It's already late,
and they're still not here.

329
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:31,477
What's with you?

330
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,312
You're so negative.

331
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:39,318
Don't be loud. You're the only one
I'll tell this to, okay.

332
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:41,987
I dreamt of Atoy again.

333
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,532
Yes. He told me I did very well.

334
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,742
I did a good job organizing this…

335
00:13:46,825 --> 00:13:48,577
our operation, the Children of the Thread.

336
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:52,373
That's why I'm really confident

337
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:54,500
we will definitely find…

338
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:57,795
[suave theme music playing]

339
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:03,008
Tailor AFAM!

340
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:08,681
Attention, Children of the Thread.

341
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:11,850
Tailor AFAM has arrived with his family.

342
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:13,978
Thread 2 and Thread 3,

343
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:15,854
he's near your location,

344
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:17,565
so, get ready. Over.

345
00:14:18,732 --> 00:14:21,068
[music fades]

346
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:26,740
[traditional instrumental music playing]

347
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,503
<i>Hola! Buenas noches!</i>

348
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:48,637
[ominous music playing]

349
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:52,850
[in Russian] My son, won't you tell me
where you got that scar on your face?

350
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:57,688
[in Russian] Did you get in trouble?

351
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:02,318
[in English] Have you been in trouble?

352
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,529
Samir is a mama's boy.

353
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:06,447
[Kurt sniffles]

354
00:15:06,530 --> 00:15:08,824
I just remembered my own mother.

355
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:12,286
[in Russian] Mama,
can you stop doing that.?

356
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:14,580
[in Russian] You're embarrassing me.

357
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:20,210
[in English] You're sweating
in this lovely hour of the night!

358
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:25,132
[in English] A mother
cannot take care of her son?

359
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:29,887
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

360
00:15:32,514 --> 00:15:35,476
[sighs]

361
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:36,685
[suspicious music playing]

362
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:38,312
- [Lily grunts]
- Get ready.

363
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:40,397
But how, Atoy?

364
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:43,943
The lock is on the other side.
We can't reach it.

365
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:48,697
And we don't have anything to use here.

366
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:50,991
[Atoy] When they deliver the food,

367
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:53,494
they'll open the door.

368
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:55,412
That's when we'll do it.

369
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:57,581
[tense music playing]

370
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:58,874
Where's the bone?

371
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:01,210
[strains] Where's the bone?

372
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,170
[Atoy] Give it to me.

373
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:04,254
[Lily grunts]

374
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:11,804
- [lock rattles]
- [gasping]

375
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:25,359
- [music fades]
- [groans]

376
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:26,819
[henchman 1] You two.

377
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:30,030
You'll surely like this.

378
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:36,370
[ominous music playing]

379
00:16:36,453 --> 00:16:37,287
What's this?

380
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,332
This isn't food.

381
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:43,335
[henchman 1] Soil!

382
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:48,549
Didn't you enjoy your steak last night?

383
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:52,011
So now, you'll eat soil!

384
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:54,763
[tense music playing]

385
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:56,515
You, like you.

386
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:59,393
I would love to bury you underground.

387
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:02,187
Just give us the laptop!

388
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,233
[huffs]

389
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,320
[applauding]

390
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:13,449
[traditional instrumental music playing]

391
00:18:07,419 --> 00:18:10,005
[in Russian] It's awful,
this place is boring!

392
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:12,925
[in English] Don't talk like that.

393
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:17,221
[in English] You should appreciate
different cultures.

394
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:27,439
- [music fades]
- <i>Olé!</i>

395
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:33,362
[cheering, applauding]

396
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:40,244
[traditional instrumental music playing]

397
00:19:00,055 --> 00:19:02,182
Damn it!

398
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:03,475
[sneaky music playing]

399
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:06,145
There's another sleazebag.

400
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:08,188
Sleazebag? Who?

401
00:19:15,737 --> 00:19:16,989
A sleazebag indeed.

402
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:26,165
[music fades]

403
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:27,124
[henchman 1, in English] I'll go.

404
00:19:27,749 --> 00:19:32,337
[ominous music playing]

405
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:33,422
[henchman 2, in English] Eat!

406
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:36,216
I told you!

407
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,384
[Lily, in English] No, no, no, no, no!

408
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:38,719
- [in English] Stop! No! Stop!
- [in English] Eat!

409
00:19:38,802 --> 00:19:40,220
[Lily gasps]

410
00:19:40,804 --> 00:19:41,722
[in English] You want?

411
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:43,682
- [Lily, in English] No, no.
- [in English] You too! Eat!

412
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:45,142
[mumbles]

413
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:46,351
[Lily, in English] No, no, no!

414
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:49,188
- [music swells]
- [grunts]

415
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:50,689
[grunts]

416
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:56,278
[Lily panting]

417
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:58,488
[Lily gasps]

418
00:20:00,532 --> 00:20:01,783
[Lily gasping]

419
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:06,330
- [tense music playing]
- Let's go.

420
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:12,211
[in English] Okay. One, two, three, smile.

421
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:14,254
- [in English] Yes, smile!
- [camera shutter snaps]

422
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:16,173
[chuckles] <i>Mabuhay!</i>

423
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:17,341
[Kurt, in English] Wonderful.

424
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:18,967
- [in English] You're so cute!
- Oh!

425
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:20,093
[in English] Thank you so much. Oh!

426
00:20:20,177 --> 00:20:21,470
[in English] Oh, sorry!

427
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:25,182
[sneaky music playing]

428
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:29,645
How are you? <i>Buenas noches!</i>

429
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:30,687
[Karla titters]

430
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:33,106
- [Samir, in English] <i>What is your name?</i>
- [in English] Uh, Kurt.

431
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:34,775
[clears throat, coughs]

432
00:20:34,858 --> 00:20:36,068
Teous.

433
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:38,237
[in English] Uh,
very courteous staff here.

434
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,447
[Kurt, in English] I am Andrei Sokolov.

435
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:43,951
[in English] We are the Sokolov brothers.

436
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:46,203
[in English] You look familiar.

437
00:20:46,286 --> 00:20:48,163
[in English] Oh, really?

438
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:49,581
[in English] You know,
I actually get that a lot.

439
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:50,499
[in English] They, uh… [chuckles]

440
00:20:50,582 --> 00:20:52,834
[in English] They say I look like
a famous actor here in the Philippines.

441
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:54,044
[titters]

442
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:56,004
Uh, no, uh…

443
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:57,673
[suspicious music playing]

444
00:20:57,756 --> 00:21:00,509
[in English] Are you sure
you're not from Zahran?

445
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:02,302
[in English] Maybe you are Sokolov?

446
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:03,804
So-- Uh, Soko--

447
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:05,472
Sokol--

448
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,393
- [Samir] Sokolov.
- Sokolo--

449
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:10,477
- [in English] What?
- There.

450
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,397
[in English] Soko what?
No. I'm… I'm American, you know.

451
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:15,565
[in English] But Filipino at heart.

452
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:19,194
- [in English] No. You don't know him.
- [mom, in English] No, no, no, no.

453
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:22,281
[in English] Yes. He's American.
We're both American.

454
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:23,657
- Mmm-hmm.
- [in English] We just work here.

455
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:25,534
- [in English] Very American. Yes.
- [in English] Yes.

456
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:28,245
[in English] You look like
a business partner,

457
00:21:28,328 --> 00:21:29,496
- Sokolov.
- [chuckles]

458
00:21:29,579 --> 00:21:30,998
[in English] Okay.

459
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:36,837
[tense music playing]

460
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:31,475
[henchman] Where are you?

461
00:22:31,558 --> 00:22:33,518
- [music fades]
- My boss isn't here.

462
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:35,937
Only Chiro and the captives are with me,

463
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:38,065
so we can drink all night.

464
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:40,400
[tense music playing]

465
00:22:44,237 --> 00:22:46,990
We really need to get out of here
before more of them arrive.

466
00:22:49,534 --> 00:22:51,411
- [softly] Come.
- [music fades]

467
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:53,789
- [in English] Let's go.
- [mom, in English] No, I don't think…

468
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:55,207
- [in English] Come on, Mother. Come on.
- [in English] He's so American.

469
00:22:55,290 --> 00:22:56,208
- [Samir, in English] Let's go.
- [in English] Yes. Thank you.

470
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:59,711
[in English] Oh, madam! Uh, gentlemen, um,

471
00:22:59,795 --> 00:23:02,005
would you guys like a private tour?

472
00:23:02,089 --> 00:23:05,008
[in English] I could take you
to the heritage houses,

473
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:06,593
like Casa Monroy.

474
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:08,386
[in English] I would love to escort you.

475
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:10,472
[in English] Uh, it's
a very nice suggestion,

476
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:12,307
but, uh, we have to go.

477
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:14,476
[in English] It's eight o'clock.
We have dinner. I have work to do.

478
00:23:14,559 --> 00:23:17,229
- [in English] Okay? Come on, let's go.
- [in English] Hedeon, please?

479
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:20,857
[in English] But brother,
could we stay a little longer?

480
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:24,277
[in English] I want to explore more
about the beauty of this place.

481
00:23:25,112 --> 00:23:26,905
[in English] I agree. Let's go.

482
00:23:26,988 --> 00:23:28,031
[in English] Follow me.

483
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:30,617
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

484
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:45,924
The child of Thread 2 is on the move.

485
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:47,592
Let's go, to the next location.

486
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:48,593
Hurry.

487
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:50,387
Mini Thread is on the way.

488
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:52,347
[Charmi] Oh! It's beautiful.

489
00:23:52,430 --> 00:23:54,766
It's so beautiful, Sister Faye.

490
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:56,852
- Hmm.
- I wish we could always come here.

491
00:23:56,935 --> 00:24:01,064
If Mama Olga treats us
to places like this, why not?

492
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:02,524
Ibyang!

493
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:05,443
- [Ame] Ibyang!
- Sister Ame?!

494
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:07,821
- Hey!
- Hey!

495
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:12,200
[sentimental music playing]

496
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:14,411
- [electronic blipping]
- [music fades]

497
00:24:20,041 --> 00:24:22,544
[tense music playing]

498
00:24:22,627 --> 00:24:24,421
[cackles, in English] Surprise!

499
00:24:24,504 --> 00:24:26,798
[in English] I will kill you.

500
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:28,175
[grunts]

501
00:24:30,802 --> 00:24:32,053
[in English] Where is my brother?!

502
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:36,099
